# The primitive objects and relations of synthetic geometry, the structured vocabulary the geometric axioms and theorems
# are written over (see the hyperbolic axiom file and note/library/seed/proof-checking/08-structured-rule-dsl). Points
# are sites; the constructors bond, beam, bend, and face build segments, rays, angles, and triangles (all carried as one
# figure type, so the congruence relation is uniform); and the relations twin (congruent), mean (between), and meet
# (incident) are the predicates the axioms postulate. Every term is a 4-letter head with structured arguments.

# A site: a point, the atom of geometry.
form site
  link place, note private

# A line: a straight one-dimensional figure.
form line
  link place, note private

# A figure: any constructed shape (a segment, ray, angle, or triangle), the thing congruence compares.
form figure
  link place, note private

# bond: the segment from site a to site b.
task bond
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  like figure
  send back
    make figure

# beam: the ray from site a through site b.
task beam
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  like figure
  send back
    make figure

# bend: the angle at site b, from site a to site c.
task bend
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  take c, like site
  like figure
  send back
    make figure

# face: the triangle on sites a, b, c.
task face
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  take c, like site
  like figure
  send back
    make figure

# twin: the congruence relation, true when two figures are congruent.
task twin
  take left, like figure
  take rest, like figure
  like wave
  send back
    wave true

# mean: the betweenness relation, true when site b lies between sites a and c.
task mean
  take a, like site
  take b, like site
  take c, like site
  like wave
  send back
    wave true

# meet: the incidence relation, true when a site lies on a line.
task meet
  take a, like site
  take here, like line
  like wave
  send back
    wave true
